  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v9.1.0: Public packages, content type display texts, search sort order, Markdown images and tables\n\n**Breaking for the CMS UI package**\n- The npm package is renamed from `@ark/cms` to `@arkframework/cms` (and `@ark/cms/client` to `@arkframework/cms/client`). Change the dependency and the imports. To install a release candidate, map the scope to the cms-packages feed in `.npmrc`: `@arkframework:registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/antonkronosjo/CMS/_packaging/cms-packages/npm/registry/`.\n\n**New**\n- Public packages: stable versions are published to nuget.org (`Ark.Framework.*`) and npmjs.org (`@arkframework/cms`), so a site needs no feed for them. Release candidates stay on the cms-packages feed.\n- Release notes: every package carries its release's notes (`<releaseNotes>` in the `.nuspec`), shown on nuget.org.\n- Content type display texts: `[DisplayText(language, name)]` on a content type, settings type, property or tab (`Tab = \"...\"`), repeatable per CMS language, with `Description`, and `Group` on a content type. The API sends them as `displayTexts` on `GET /api/content/types`, the creation, update and settings schemas and `GET /api/settings`. The CMS UI shows them - create picker names, descriptions and groups, field labels and help texts, tab and type names - before the site's `resources`.\n- Search sort order: `o.Sorts` on `MapArkSearch` lists the index fields visitors may sort by, such as `SearchSchema.FirstPublishedField`. `GET /api/search?sort={field}&desc=true` picks one; without `sort` the order is best match first, as before. A sort the site didn't allow is a 400; a field in `o.Sorts` that can't be sorted on stops the site at startup. `searchContent` in `@arkframework/cms/client` takes `sort` and `desc`.\n\n**Fixed**\n- The CMS Markdown editor keeps images, GFM tables and raw HTML. Before, editing any text saved it without its images and tables, and with its HTML escaped. A table may be saved reformatted, with the same cells.\n\n**Docs**\n- Guide: a section on the CMS editor UI, and where stable versions and release candidates come from.\n\nNo migrations.",
